\u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dcf\u0d82 \u0dc3\u0db8\u0d9f \u0d91\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dd4\u0dc4\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dd4 \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0d9c\u0dda\u0dc1 \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dc0 \u0d89\u0dad\u0dcf \u0dbb\u0dc5\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dc4\u0dd0\u0d9a.\n\nPage 1 of 3\n\nWeather forecast for multi-day boats For the sea areas in between 20N - 10S and 60E-100E (Issued at 07.00 a.m. on 07 January 2026, for next 24 hours)\n\nSea Areas Around the island\n\nBay of Bengal\n\nThe low-pressure area in the Bay of Bengal, to the southeast of the Sri Lanka is likely intensify into a depression during next 12 hours. During the next few days, heavy thundershowers are expected in the sea areas bounded by the 01\u00b0N to 12\u00b0N and 80\u00b0E to 90\u00b0E (01\u00b0N\u201312\u00b0N, 80\u00b0E\u201390\u00b0E). Wind speeds may increase at times up to 60\u201370 kmph, and sea conditions are likely to become rough in these areas. Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to these sea areas until further notice. Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move away from the affected sea areas.\n\nThe low-pressure area in the Bay of Bengal, to the southeast of the Sri Lanka is likely intensify into a depression during next 12 hours. This system is expected to move west-northwestwards, towards the east coast of the island.\n\nNaval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep and shallow sea areas extending from Kankasanthurai to Hambantota via Trincomalee and Pottuvil from 07th January until further notice. Navel and fishing communities are requested to pay attention to further advisories issued by the Meteorological Department in this regard. Condition of Rain:"
