nity of Sri Lanka is likely to develop into a low-pressure area around 11th of May. Therefore, the prevailing showery conditions over the island are expected to continue during the next few days. Cloudy skies are expected over most parts of the island.\n\nShowers or thundershowers will occur at most places of the island after 1.00 pm. Heavy falls above 100 mm are likely at some places.\n\nShowers are likely in the Western, Southern, Eastern and Northern provinces during the morning too.\n\nThe general public is kindly requested to take adequate precautions to minimize damage caused by temporary localized strong winds and lightning during thundershowers.\n\n\u0dc1\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0db3\u0dc4\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0d85\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba GENERAL WEATHER FORECAST FOR SRI LANKA \u0da2\u0ddc\u0dad\u0dd2\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba\u0ddc \u0db8\u0db0\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0ddc\u0db1\u0db1\u0dda, \u0d85\u0db1\u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dd2 \u0d85\u0d82\u0dc1\u0dba \u0db8\u0d9c\u0dd2\u0dda \u0db1\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf\u0dd2 Issued by Forecasting Division, National Meteorological Centre\n\nDate : 10-May-2026\n\nCity Temperature (0C) Relative Humidity (%) Weather Max Min Max Min Anuradhapura 33 25 95 60 Showers or thundershowers after 2.00p.m Batticaloa 32 26 95 70 Showers or thundershowers"
