    "chunk_text": "==== BLOCKS ====\n\nColor: -Red Waning (Take action)\n\nColor: -Amber Advisory (Be prepared)\n\nColor: -Green Threat is over\n\nBulletin No: 01 LRW/26/05/15/01 COLOR: Red\n\nWarning for Heavy Rain Issued by the Natural Hazards Early Warning Centre Issued at 09.30 a.m. on 15 May 2026 valid for the period until 08.30 a.m. 16 May 2026\n\nFor Western, Sabaragamuwa, North-western provinces Galle and Matara\n\ndistricts.\n\nTake action!\n\nThe low-pressure area located northeast of the Sri Lanka, still persist. This system is expected to move away from Sri Lanka during the next 36 hours according to the latest weather analysis based on May 15th morning.\n\nVery heavy showers about 150mm are likely at some places in Western, Sabaragamuwa and North-western provinces. Heavy showers above 100mm are likely at some places in and in Galle and Matara districts. Therefore, general public is advised to take adequate precautions to minimize damages caused by heavy rain, strong winds and lightning during thundershowers. Situation: Reported rainfall (currently received) from 08.30 a.m. on 14.05.2026 to 08.30 a.m. on 15.05.2026 given below.\n\nAutomatic Weather Station Districts Rainfall (mm)\n\nPenrith Estate, Avissawella Colombo 175.0\n\nVeyangoda Gampaha 162.0\n\nKirindiwela Gampaha 157.0\n\nPambegama Estate Kegalle 135.0\n\nTalduwa Kegalle 131.0\n\nMaliboda Kegalle 125.5"
